{
  "dom_id": "step-q111185",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(3,6)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=\\frac{1}{3}f(x)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The function $y=\\frac{1}{3}f(x)$ represents a compression of the function $y=f(x)$ by a factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the point $(3,6)$ on $f(x)$ is mapped to the point $(3,\\frac{6}{3})=(3,2),$ and this point must lie on the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{3}f(x).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
